+// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+//  M0 INTEGRATION GATE — SG_TUNED_MB_PROJ_WGMMA  (DEFAULT OFF → byte-identical).
+//
+//  Wires the dormant M0 wgmma-projection infra above into fused_mamba_megakernel_tc.
+//  This is the SCAFFOLD half of the integration (the decoder's SG_TUNED_DEC_DW_STAGE
+//  pattern): it gates the WORKSPACE so the host sizer (mb_tc_workspace_floats) and
+//  the kernel carve advance by the SAME gated amount — the ViT-IMA invariant. The
+//  kernel-BODY rewire (running a token-tile fwd that MATERIALIZES the projection
+//  acts to the MbActs HBM region, then the output-stationary dW phase) is the
+//  remaining step and is documented as GPU-iteration-gated below — it is NOT
+//  enabled by this macro flipping ON, because it would change the fp32 dW
+//  accumulation order (single-sample kSeq reduce → full-T K-contraction) and so
+//  MUST be re-validated against the fp64 oracle on real silicon (parity is NOT
+//  provable CPU-side). When OFF (the default) NOTHING here is instantiated: every
+//  sizer term is 0, the kernel carve is gated to match → the production d=128
+//  build is byte-for-byte unchanged (proven via PTX diff).
+//
